        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Max Joseph, Meaghan Oppenheimer, Richard Silverman, Zac Efron, Emily Ratajkowski, Wes Bentley, Robin Thicke\n- Works: We Are Your Friends, \"Blurred Lines\"\n- Places: London, California, Los Angeles\n- Topics: film production, music industry, celebrity biography, controversy\n\nFacts:\n- Emily Ratajkowski was born to American parents in London and was raised primarily in California.\n- In 2013, Emily Ratajkowski rose to prominence after appearing in Robin Thicke's \"Blurred Lines\" music video.\n- In 2013, Robin Thicke's \"Blurred Lines\" became the number one song of the year in several countries and attracted controversy over its purportedly sexist content.\n- We Are Your Friends is a 2015 drama film directed by Max Joseph in his directorial debut.\n- We Are Your Friends was written by Max Joseph and Meaghan Oppenheimer from a story by Richard Silverman.\n- We Are Your Friends stars Zac Efron, Emily Ratajkowski, and Wes Bentley.\n- We Are Your Friends follows a young Los Angeles DJ trying to succeed in the music industry and navigate life with his friends.",
